{"uid":"d082cdf69f7e195","name":"test_an_approach_end_review_also_inserts_the_remedy_task","fullName":"tests.test_midrun_refuted_continues#test_an_approach_end_review_also_inserts_the_remedy_task","historyId":"7faa3e17a4b4cf402017957fe34f741e","time":{"start":1791969163905,"stop":1791969163929,"duration":24},"description":"PRD requirement D.2 (task 019, #220) supersedes this node's earlier\n    pin. Until this task the `mid_run` guard `_insert_refuted_remedy_tasks`\n    sat behind meant an ordinary, run-ending review pass (`mid_run=False`)\n    inserted no remedy task at all -- the earlier version of this node\n    pinned exactly that absence, reasoning that nothing at approach-end\n    guaranteed the inserted task would ever be worked (accept could\n    `_finish(\"succeeded\", ...)` over it, archive-and-replan could discard\n    it, and only a curable rejection's cure pass was known to reach it).\n\n    Requirement D.1 (task 018) removed that gap by giving\n    `_terminal_success_blockers()` a THIRD blocker for any non-terminal\n    `review-cure`-origin task: the same protection steering-origin tasks\n    already had. With that blocker in place, requirement D.2 (this task)\n    lifted the `mid_run` guard itself -- `_review_verdict` now calls\n    `_insert_refuted_remedy_tasks` unconditionally, so a REFUTED\n    `substance` remedy becomes work on an approach-end review exactly as it\n    already did on the mid-run adjudication episode\n    (`test_the_substance_remedy_becomes_a_pending_cure_task_through_the_\n    real_engine` above), and the accept branch that used to strand it is\n    now caught by that same blocker before the run can go terminal.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>PRD requirement D.2 (task 019, #220) supersedes this node's earlier<br />\npin. Until this task the <code>mid_run</code> guard <code>_insert_refuted_remedy_tasks</code><br />\nsat behind meant an ordinary, run-ending review pass (<code>mid_run=False</code>)<br />\ninserted no remedy task at all -- the earlier version of this node<br />\npinned exactly that absence, reasoning that nothing at approach-end<br />\nguaranteed the inserted task would ever be worked (accept could<br />\n<code>_finish(&quot;succeeded&quot;, ...)</code> over it, archive-and-replan could discard<br />\nit, and only a curable rejection's cure pass was known to reach it).</p>\n<pre><code>Requirement D.1 (task 018) removed that gap by giving\n`_terminal_success_blockers()` a THIRD blocker for any non-terminal\n`review-cure`-origin task: the same protection steering-origin tasks\nalready had. With that blocker in place, requirement D.2 (this task)\nlifted the `mid_run` guard itself -- `_review_verdict` now calls\n`_insert_refuted_remedy_tasks` unconditionally, so a REFUTED\n`substance` remedy becomes work on an approach-end review exactly as it\nalready did on the mid-run adjudication episode\n(`test_the_substance_remedy_becomes_a_pending_cure_task_through_the_\nreal_engine` above), and the accept branch that used to strand it is\nnow caught by that same blocker before the run can go terminal.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791968776876,"stop":1791968776877,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791968776877,"stop":1791968776877,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791969163858,"stop":1791969163858,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasC